  "question": {
    "text": "The parabolas <math><msub><mrow><mi>C</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mo>:</mo><msup><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>a</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> and <math><msub><mrow><mi>C</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mo>:</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><msup><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>a</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> intersect at two distinct points <math><mi>A</mi></math> and <math><mi>B</mi><mo>.</mo></math> If the slope of the tangent at <math><mi>A</mi></math> on <math><msub><mrow><mi>C</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math> is same as the slope of the normal at <math><mi>B</mi></math> on <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;, then the value of k&nbsp;is equal to",
    "image": null
  },
